# Tier 4: Scenarios And MCP Protocol Assertions
File: ootail/qa/tier4_scenarios.oot

Status: ACTIVE. Validates end-to-end agent and system workflows.

## Scope

Verifies Model Context Protocol stdio transport frames, multi-turn
sessions, systemd journal integration, and live rotation scenarios.

## MCP Protocol Invariants

The MCP server runs over stdio with newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 frames.
Zero ambient authority is granted; all operations use explicit capabilities.

| ID | Invocation | Expectation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| T4-01 | `initialize` frame | returns protocolVersion 2024-11-05 and serverInfo |
| T4-02 | `notifications/initialized` | silent acknowledgment, ready for calls |
| T4-03 | `ping` frame | returns empty result object |
| T4-04 | `tools/list` frame | declares `tail_file` and `tail_stream` tools |
| T4-05 | `tools/call` tail_file lines | returns trailing lines from file target |
| T4-06 | `tools/call` tail_file bytes | returns trailing bytes from file target |
| T4-07 | `tools/call` tail_file +offset | returns lines from start offset |
| T4-08 | `tools/call` tail_stream lines | windows lines from in-memory string |
| T4-09 | `tools/call` unknown tool | returns JSON-RPC error -32601 |
| T4-10 | `tools/call` missing path | returns JSON-RPC error -32602 |
| T4-11 | `shutdown` frame | returns null result and closes session |

## Systemd & Streaming Scenarios

| ID | Invocation | Expectation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| T4-12 | `journalctl -n 5 \| ootail -n 3` | stream journalctl output through tail window |
| T4-13 | inotify append cycle | follower yields appended lines and sleeps |
| T4-14 | file truncate cycle | follower reports truncation notice and resets offset |

## Invariant Under Test

An LLM agent receives structured, escaped, bounded output suitable for context windows.
Transport loops handle disconnections cleanly without zombie processes.
